arxiv:2601.19397.abstract:
We study the processes \(
u_{	au}nightarrow\Lambda_{c}	au^{-}(\pi^{-}
u_{	au})\) and \({\overline{
u}}_{	au}pightarrow\Lambda	au^{+}(\pi^{+}{\overline{
u}}_{	au})\), with particular emphasis on the pion energy and angular distributions, as a possible signal for lepton flavor universality violation, and in general of physics beyond the Standard Model (SM), as well as a sensitive probe of the \(	au\) polarization vector. We work within an effective low-energy extension of the SM with all dimension-six four-fermion operators. In this framework, complex Wilson coefficients which encode new physics can generate \(CP\)-violating contributions. We propose an observable that provides a genuine \(CP\)-odd signal due to its sensitivity to particular transverse components of the \(	au\) polarization vector. Namely, we show that the asymmetry in the azimuthal-angle distribution of the pion in the decay \(	au^{\pm}ightarrow\pi^{\pm}
u_{	au}\) constitutes a smoking-gun prediction of such a beyond the SM scenario. We estimate the strength of this effect extrapolating nucleon-hyperon form factors recently obtained from lattice QCD calculations.

