u} + 
u)) = 7.05$ cpd/100t and $R(^{210}$Bi$) = 6$ cpd/100t. We performed MC pseudo-experiments and found that we do not have enough statistics and need to know the bismuth concentration in the scintillator for definite measurement of potassium abundance in the Earth. The possibility of building a next-generation detector for looking for the $^{40}$K-geo-($ ar{
